  "reviews": [
    {
      "author_name": "Diana Dvorská",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107783948626034549522/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocL7FVYe9sqPBD9PF0e0v8h0iLdXo0eW9ndUltJQEYcEsLnv7g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
      "rating": 5,
      "relative_time_description": "in the last week",
      "text": "Came early in the morning around 8 AM, and they weren’t fully stocked yet—but I grabbed the only vegan option I saw from the onigiri section, and it was a 10/10! Super fresh and flavorful. Can’t wait to come back when they’re fully stocked to try more.",
      "time": 1750553195,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "Kris Gonzalez",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104018129511324535439/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU_2bn-_AzqmdYkC_m_svo25T7GtkLza4VZYYE9TU1UaUxoyifk=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
      "rating": 5,
      "relative_time_description": "3 months ago",
      "text": "I went here to get onigiri after craving it for around a week. The food I ate here was SO GOOD. First, the store isn’t too far of a walk from the Grand Central station when you go inside the store looks to be pretty small, and although it is small it’s bigger than when it first appears. The photo shows I ate while I went around in Manhattan. I got shrimp tempura, ume, eel, salmon, chashew pork (I’m unsure of the spelling), spam musubi I believe it’s called, and some more stuff. Almost everything I bought was under 5$ and came up to 34$. And I can stay without a doubt that the food is most definitely worth the money. The shrimp tempura was delicious. The ume I believe it is, wasn’t really my thing but that’s not the fault of the food. The staff were very nice and that store was very clean and well taken care of. Normally, I don’t write reviews for places I’ve gone, but this is how good at this spot is I had to write about it. One thing I want to really highlight is the takoyaki octopus balls, they were near the middle of the store I was curious so I got them. now, of course, this is up to personal taste for but for me these things literally had me yelling with how good they were and I’m not even joking. The texture was very nice. It was chewy. The sauce was good. The stuff that was on It was delicious. The inside had like a small piece of octopus in it. All around one of my favorite things for that store and will definitely be buying the next time I go. 10/10 this store is fantastic.",
      "time": 1742668579,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "Jill Chen",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101682339028256340709/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXp9PHIDV5aG2WyWoB8npPlK1SbM-pjewbLNuw2z6vwwL70Zwk=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
      "rating": 1,
      "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
      "text": "Went there today around 11am. Staff are very friendly, but the food is dirty. Bought 4 rice balls, when I eat them I saw something in the rice balls. See the pictures attached. I use chopsticks to make it look clear and then moved it to another rice balls to take pictures. What if I didn’t see it and eat it by accident?? Won’t be back again!",
      "time": 1748448888,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "Syaif muhami shidiq (Kukirakira)",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112062538900677893005/reviews",
      "language": "en",
      "original_language": "en",
      "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXt0GUDaLFtHe3uHkeI-h9FQp8Sra1zxoDevxRDn4qY6j0KxpzsfA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
      "rating": 4,
      "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
      "text": "Omusubi Gonbei is my go-to spot for quick, delicious Japanese comfort food. Their onigiri bombs are absolutely the highlight—crispy on the outside with warm, flavorful fillings that range from classic tuna mayo to bold, spicy options. The variety is impressive, and everything is made fresh with high-quality ingredients. Beyond onigiri, they also offer a nice selection of hot foods like karaage and miso soup, which make for a complete and satisfying meal. The drink options are also great, from bottled teas to Japanese sodas, giving you plenty of choices to pair with your meal.\n\nThe space is clean and efficient, perfect for grab-and-go or a casual dine-in. My only minor complaint is that they no longer offer free mayo or chili flakes, which used to add a great finishing touch to the onigiri. Still, the food more than makes up for it with its flavor and consistency. If you’re craving Japanese rice balls or just looking for something comforting and tasty, this place never misses.",
      "time": 1746806028,
      "translated": false
    },
    {
      "author_name": "R",
      "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114428392323157797265/reviews",
